  "scientific_assessment": {
    "falsifiable_scientific_hypothesis": "HYPOTHESIS F1728-H2-CASE2: Native Abaqus UNIFORM_ERROR remeshing driven by linear-elastic pre-analysis (Step-1) will produce a mesh highly refined at the notch root but coarse across the notch-to-hole ligament. Conversely, driving adaptive remeshing from an authentic phase-field donor checkpoint at or near peak load (Step-2 peak, u2 ~ 0.00729 mm, d_max ~ 0.58) provides the physical Cauchy-stress redistribution and steep stress jumps required to natively allocate elements resolving h <= l0/2 along the entire oblique fracture corridor into the hole flank without manual corridor seeding.",
    "phase_field_evolution_behavior": "In the authentic coarse phase-field simulation (PK_HOLE_COARSE_JOB1.odb), Step-1 end (u2 = 0.0050 mm) remains in the precritical regime (d_max = 0.1691, only 4 damaged elements). In Step-2, pre-peak hardening drives active damage localization directly along the oblique ligament towards the hole. At peak load (u2 = 0.00729 mm, F_max = 0.7310 kN), peak damage reaches d = 0.5798 with 48 actively softening elements bridging the notch tip towards the hole boundary. At Step-2 end (u2 = 0.00959 mm), full fracture penetration is achieved (d_max = 0.9976, 20 broken elements).",
    "preanalysis_behavior": "Under linear-elastic pre-analysis (Step-1, u2 = 0.005 mm), MISESERI strongly concentrates at the notch tip (max = 107.39 MPa, mean in tip core = 68.42 MPa, 17.6x higher than bulk 3.88 MPa). However, along the prospective oblique crack path towards the hole flank (0.65, 0.55), MISESERI decays to 15-25 MPa, and at the hole flank itself mean error is only 12.18 MPa. This means that, exactly as in Case 1, native UNIFORM_ERROR remeshing on linear-elastic pre-analysis will refine the notch tip but leave the hole-interaction ligament under-refined.",
    "recommended_next_execution_dependency": "1. For immediate Stage D pilot parity evaluation, qualify native remeshing under Step-1 elastic pre-analysis to establish baseline technical parity and document the exact spatial decay.\n2. For complete crack-corridor refinement, qualify the Step-2 peak-load checkpoint (u2 = 0.00729 mm) from PK_HOLE_COARSE_JOB1.odb using companion stress recovery."
  },
